            "review_text": "DirtyPierreOnTour\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam12577 contributions\n1\nThe only place in the entire HCMC that serves good Char Kway Teow\nJun 2016 • Solo\nI have eaten here many times since 2009 then I couldn't remember how to find this place again until just recently.\nI am so glad I found it again as I really miss my Char Kway Teow. It is probably my favourite Malaysian/Singaporean noodle dish. It consists of flat rice noodles stir fried with black soy sauce and is can be with tender marinated beef, slices of sweet roast pork or my favourite, succulent King Prawns.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten June 28, 2016",
